           <li>Finishing or modifying the structure containing repaired or replaced product.</li>
           <li></li>
           <li>Products that have not been paid for in full.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">II. Minor imperfections in the product:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
           <li>Minor imperfections in the panel and/or frame graining or color.</li>
           <li>Variations in wood grain, color, texture or natural characteristics.</li>
           <li>Variations or unsatisfactory results in gloss levels, texture or appearance resulting from the field application of paint or other finishing material.</li>
           <li>Minor imperfections in glass that do not affect the product’s structural integrity or significantly obscure vision (including textures, swirls and air bubbles in decorative glass).</li>
           <li>Minor variations in glass color.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">III. Additionally, ETO is not responsible for, and makes no warranty with respect to:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
           <li>Rustic alder surface checks which are less than 1/8” in width and 5” long.</li>
           <li>Variation in thickness, width, or length less than the industry standards.</li>
           <li>Damage resulting from attempts to repair doors by persons other than ETO Doors or its designated representative. Knot size, shape or placement or any natural variation in color or texture of the wood.</li>
           <li>Knife, molder or shaper marks which do not impair the dimensional integrity of the door.</li>
           <li>Damage caused by or resulting from improper machining by the pre-hanger.</li>
           <li>Warping of any door within the tolerances stated in Section I of this Disclaimer above.</li>
           <li>Problems due to misuse or abuse of the door.</li>
           <li>Variation or unsatisfactory results in sheen or texture resulting from the field application of paint, stain or lacquer or any other finishing material or damage caused by extreme temperature.</li>
           <li>Expansion and contraction of the door and other changes in form due to environmental conditions, including without limitation changes in moisture, temperature and humidity.</li>
           <li>Panel shrinkage and misalignment, which leaves an unstained line along the edge of the panel (may be caused by fluctuations or differences in temperature and humidity).</li>
           <li>Bowing or misalignment in the frame or jamb in which the door panel is hung, problems related to water and/or air infiltration due to improper assembly or installation.</li>
           <li>Improper installation of hardware.</li>
           <li>Discoloration or rusting caused by decorative metal accent options (such as grilles, clavos, straps, etc.) or hardware or inserts (such as locksets, door handles, strikes, etc.).</li>
           <li>Using an interior door in an exterior application.</li>
           <li>Door installed in a building before mudding and taping is dried and complete.</li>
           <li>Acceptable characteristics include variations in color, stain, wood grain, grain appearance, unlimited tight knots and unlimited worm holes. These variations in the product are completely normal.</li>
           <li>Modifying an ETO Door will also void the warranty. Modifying includes excessive trimming, removing panels, v-grooving damage (v-grooves in excess of 3/8" wide and 3/16" deep), and distressing damage. Allowable trimming on an ETO Door is ½” from the sides of the door and the top of the door and 1” from the bottom of the door.</li>
           <li>Any visible defect or mistake in shipment that is apparent on receipt and is reported to ETO Doors more than 24 hours after receipt or after the product is machined or installed.</li>
           <li>Bowing Checking and Warping: Exposure to the environment may cause bowing checking and/or cracking. These are not defects. They are only unforeseen and uncontrollable characteristics of natural wood. It is the sole responsibility of the buyer and the end user to select the type of material and/or door that will offer the best results and longevity in each climate and/or environment.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">IV. Installation inconsistent with ETO Installation Instructions:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
           <li>Damage resulting in whole or in part from installation inconsistent with ETO’s Installation Instructions.</li>
           <li>Altered or reinstalled products.</li>
           <li>Products used in non-vertical glazing applications.</li>
           <li>Combinations not built by ETO or not built in accordance with ETO’s recommendations for mulling and combining ETO products.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">ADDITIONAL WARRANTY INFORMATION</p>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">I. NFRC Standards.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">ETO products labeled with the National Fenestration Rating Council (NFRC) Energy Performance label are tested in accordance with NFRC standards. NFRC ratings are based on a combination of computer simulations and physical testing of product samples. For details on NFRC energy performance ratings, go to NFRC.org.</p>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">II. Entire Agreement.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">With the exception of a written statement signed by an authorized ETO representative, this Limited Warranty and all terms contained herein constitutes the entire agreement between ETO/Seller and Buyer/User. This Limited Warranty, including all Limitations of Liability contained herein, are made a part of any such written agreement, unless expressly excluded therein. By purchasing or using the product covered by this Limited Warranty, Buyer and User agree that they are not relying on any oral statements made by anyone that are in any way contrary to this Limited Warranty.</p>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">III. No Amendment Except in Writing.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">ETO and Seller offer this product, and Buyer and User accept it, subject to the foregoing Warranty, which may be modified only by written agreement signed by a duly authorized representative of ETO.</p>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">IV. Venue and Choice of Law</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">Any persons and entities that choose to enforce this warranty agree that all matters, disputes, or transactions arising from the use of this warranty shall be governed by California law, without regard to its conflict-of-laws principles, and shall be within the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts located in Los Angeles, California. Any dispute under this agreement shall have venue in the courts of Los Angeles, CA.</p>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">V. Severability</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">If any part of this warranty is unlawful, void or unenforceable, that part will be deemed severable and will not affect the validity and enforceability of remaining provisions. ETO Doors Corp. may revise this warranty at any time by updating this document. Any revision applies prospectively only, to products sold on or after the effective date of the revision; the version of this Limited Warranty in effect on the date of sale governs that sale.</p>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">VI. CLAIMS UNDER THESE WARRANTIES</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">Prompt Notice of Claim.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">Within the warranty period, Buyer or User shall notify ETO immediately and in no case more than thirty (30) days after any defect or other basis of a claim covered by these Limited Warranties is discovered or should have been discovered, and in no event after expiration of the one (1) year warranty period. Any claims otherwise covered by the foregoing warranties, but for which ETO did not receive notice within that period, shall be barred.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">Additional Claims Related Issues and Policies:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
           <li>Missing Items: All missing items or incomplete deliveries must be reported within forty-eight (48) hours (two (2) days) from receipt of material. ETO Doors cannot be responsible for materials lost, stolen, or damaged while on site. We will reject all claims for missing items after forty-eight (48) hours of receipt.</li>
           <li>Product Damage (not visible from outside packaging): All such concealed product damage must be reported within forty-eight (48) hours (two (2) days) from receipt of material. Customer is not to stain, prep, or modify damaged product whatsoever; any modification made to a damaged item will render a claim null and void.</li>
           <li>Freight Damage and Handling: Any package, crate, pallet, or parcel that is visibly damaged, or the contents within appear to be damaged in freight, must be noted on the bill of lading at the time the material is received and delivery from carrier is to be refused.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">Limited Warranty Claim Procedure.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">Claims under these Limited Warranties may be made in writing to ETO Doors Corp., Claims Department, 1340 E. 6th Street, Los Angeles, CA 90021, or by calling for service at 213-622-2003. Claims to ETO should include the following information:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
           <li>Claimant’s name, address and phone number, and the installation address (if different);</li>
           <li>A description of the product, purchase price, date and location of purchase, and copies of invoices;</li>
           <li>A description of the product concerns (photos may be included); and</li>
           <li>A brief summary of attempts made to address the concerns; and</li>
           <li>A completed ETO Doors Claim Form.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">VII. INQUIRIES.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;">If you have any questions regarding any portion of this Warranty, or if you wish to inquire, regarding rights of use not explicitly granted herein, please direct questions via email to sales@etodoors.com.</p>
